#
# samples/modelblaster_pext's Kconfig, for the same reason and with the same meaning: this
# app links THE SAME generated kernels.c, which reads CONFIG_MB_PEXT out of autoconf.h to
# decide whether pext.h emits real custom-0 encodings or its bit-identical software model.
# A live transcript must be the same arithmetic as the measured one, so this is =y here.

mainmenu "Moonshine, live -- record from the microphone and transcribe on the board"

config MB_PEXT
	bool "Build the ModelBlaster kernels against the MBP extension"
	default y
	help
	  Emit the real MBP.DOT8 / MBP.MAX8 / MBP.QMUL / MBP.CLIP8 encodings
	  (custom-0, opcode 0x0b) instead of pext.h's software model.

	  THE EXTENSION EXISTS ON HART 0 ONLY.  Any thread that reaches a curated
	  pext kernel must be on CPU 0 or it takes an illegal-instruction trap.
	  See PEXT_SPEC.md section 7.

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
